File Index

/dslToAnsi.ts
Purpose: Converts DSL color codes to ANSI escape sequences for terminal rendering.

/expand-global-vars.ts
Purpose: Expands global variables in match text while validating non-empty results.

/get-global-vars.ts
Purpose: Retrieves global variable values by key name from the global variables snapshot.

/globalRuntime.ts
Purpose: Manages global script execution across JavaScript, TypeScript, Lua, and Python languages with caching and invalidation.

/globalScriptsStore.ts
Purpose: Manages persistent storage and caching of global scripts and variables for user-defined code execution. Also owns the cloud shape: GlobalScriptBucket plus getAllGlobalScriptBuckets/replaceGlobalScriptBuckets, kept here so the wire and storage shapes stay defined side by side. getAllGlobalScriptBuckets reads localStorage DIRECTLY rather than the cache — a connection this session never opened was never cached, and skipping it would silently drop that connection's globals on the next save. A load only overwrites buckets the cloud actually returned, so a connection that exists locally but not in the cloud keeps its globals. setGlobalVar/deleteGlobalVar debounce the actual disk write per connection key (pendingVarsWrite) so a trigger firing per matched line doesn't call the blocking localStorage.setItem on every one — varsCache/varsRawCache still update synchronously, and getGlobalVarsSnapshot trusts the cache over a stale on-disk read while a write is pending, so nothing reads a torn/lagging value.

/luaRuntime.ts
Purpose: Provides a Lua runtime environment that bridges JavaScript APIs for user scripts. As of 2026-08-15, `event` (trigger/alias/timer context) is bridged as a Lua table via a hand-rolled recursive pushJsValue helper — fengari has no built-in JS<->Lua remapper (unlike Skulpt's ffi.remapToPy). Mobile's features/scripts/lua-runtime.ts is the matching implementation; keep the two in step or Lua scripts stop being portable.

/pythonRuntime.ts
Purpose: Enables Python script execution with typed Skulpt integration and API bridging. Two defects fixed 2026-08-01, both long-lived because bridge calls (sendCommand/log) kept working while everything else silently did not: `read()` threw unconditionally, breaking every `import` AND `print()` (Skulpt reaches for `sys` to get at stdout) — it now serves Skulpt's bundled stdlib, which cannot reach a real filesystem; and global modules were loaded under a name but registered by importMainWithBody as `__main__`, so calling in via `import <name> as g` never resolved — loadPythonModuleBody now keeps the returned module OBJECT and callPythonModuleFunction reads attributes off it, which also stops interpolating a caller-supplied function name into generated Python. As of 2026-08-15, `event` (trigger/alias/timer context) is also bridged, remapped via sk.ffi.remapToPy into a Python dict (`event["payload"]["text"]`) — it previously was NOT registered as a builtin even though runtime.ts's JS/TS path always exposed it, so a translated TS trigger script referencing `event`/`api.event` silently NameError'd in Python. Covered by pythonRuntime.test.ts (real Skulpt, not mocks). Mobile's features/scripts/python-runtime.ts is the matching implementation; keep the two in step or Python scripts stop being portable.

/runtime.ts
